mca:hwloc:base:param:hwloc_base_mem_bind_failure_action:help:What Open MPI will do if it explicitly tries to bind memory to a specific NUMA location, and fails.  Note that this is a different case than the general allocation policy described by hwloc_base_alloc_policy.  A value of "silent" means that Open MPI will proceed without comment. A value of "warn" means that Open MPI will warn the first time this happens, but allow the job to continue (possibly with degraded performance).  A value of "error" means that Open MPI will abort the job if this happens.
